# A function with NO return statement, called where a VALUE is wanted.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that the common shape of this call was always
# right and the uncommon ones were always wrong, which is why it survived. A
# void function called as a STATEMENT compiles to a direct C call; called in a
# value context it fell through to the BUILTIN emission path, which resolves
# the name dynamically out of the env — and a user function is a `static` C
# function that is never in the env, so the lookup always failed:
#
#   VM   prints, yields null, rc 0
#   AOT  aot: undefined function 'shout', rc 1
#
# The VM's rule is that a function falling off its end yields null, so the call
# still happens and answers null.
#
# THREE SITES had to agree, and each was found by a separate review round
# rather than by enumerating the shape space -- so do not read the list below
# as complete, read it as what has been caught:
#
#   emit_val            the boxed value form, `({ f(...); make_null(); })`
#   return_node_is_boxed the DECLARED type. Teaching only the emitter left
#                       `wrap` declared `double` while its body produced a
#                       null, dying at the checked unbox with a different
#                       message and the same rc 1.
#   arg_class           the CALLER's parameter inference. A void call in an
#                       argument position contributed no constraint, so the
#                       callee was declared `double` and the emitted C was
#                       `eig_g(eig_shout(...))` -- a void expression where a
#                       double is required. gcc rejected the build outright:
#                       no binary, and no `AOT:` diagnostic naming the cause.
#   the numeric PIN     which discarded arg_class's answer whenever the callee
#                       computes with the parameter anywhere in its body --
#                       so the site above was taught and then overridden.
#   widen_scan's        a void result parked in a LOCAL was not boxed evidence
#   local classifier    either; it tested only `ret == "Value*"`.
#
# Two earlier versions of this comment overclaimed and both were caught by the
# next round's review. One said "all three shapes are here" against a shape
# space nobody had enumerated; the other said the `adds`/`takes_two` pair below
# makes a fix that "simply boxes every argument" fail, which was tested and is
# FALSE -- boxing every call argument, and boxing every argument outright, both
# leave this fixture byte-identical. Boxing is semantics-preserving, so no
# output diff can catch it; that mutant is a PERFORMANCE regression and needs a
# benchmark, not a parity fixture. The pair stays because it exercises a
# numeric and a void argument in one call, which is worth covering on its own.

define shout(m) as:
    print of m

define counts(n) as:
    # no return either, but reached with a numeric argument
    print of (n * 2)

define wrap(m) as:
    # value context inside a FUNCTION body — the shape that exposed the
    # declared-type/emission disagreement
    return (shout of m)

define wrap_num(n) as:
    return (counts of n)

# the statement form, which was always correct — kept so a fix that broke it
# cannot pass
shout of "as-statement"

# value context in an ASSIGNMENT
y is (shout of "in-assign")
print of y

# value context through a function return
print of (wrap of "via-wrap")
print of (wrap_num of 21)

# the void result used where a value is genuinely consumed
vals is [(shout of "in-list"), 1]
print of vals

# and compared, which forces it through the boxed path
if (shout of "in-cond") == null:
    print of "null-as-expected"

# ARGUMENT position: the callee's parameter must be inferred BOXED from this
# site. `takes_it` has nothing else to type its parameter, so if a void call
# contributes no constraint the parameter defaults to double and the generated
# C does not compile at all.
define takes_it(n) as:
    print of n

takes_it of (shout of "as-argument")

# the same, one level indirect, and mixed with a genuinely numeric call so a
# fix that simply boxes every argument is caught by the numeric side
define adds(a) as:
    return a + 1

define takes_two(p, q) as:
    print of p
    print of q

takes_two of [(shout of "arg-1"), (adds of 41)]

# The callee COMPUTES with its parameter, which pins it numeric. That pin used
# to win over the boxed verdict above, so this is the shape that fails to BUILD
# rather than merely printing the wrong thing. The `n == null` guard is why the
# program is correct in the VM and is exactly what makes the pin wrong.
define guarded(n) as:
    if n == null:
        print of "guarded-null"
    else:
        print of (n * 2)

guarded of 5
guarded of (shout of "pinned-arg")

# A void result parked in a LOCAL, then passed on: the local must be boxed
# evidence too. This one built and then died at the checked unbox.
#
# `solo_taker` is called from exactly ONE site and that site passes the local,
# so the local classifier is the only evidence about its parameter. Routing it
# through `takes_it` instead proved nothing: `takes_it` is already boxed by its
# direct void-call site above, so reverting the local fix left the fixture
# green. A shared callee hides the very thing this case is for.
define solo_taker(p) as:
    print of p

solo is (shout of "via-local")
solo_taker of solo
